{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires","id":1032109,"title":"Baron samedi, dreamspeakers, vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-15T06:48:46-08:00","id":1032109,"title":"Baron samedi, dreamspeakers, vampires","content":"I've run into a dilemma. <br /> <br /> My dreamspeaker is a Haitian bokor with a deep affinity for the Loa. Lately, he's been asking them for help and to become his allies and so on. I've been interested in soliciting baron samedi, the Haitian deity of death as one of his allies. <br /> <br /> <br /> Problem is, apparently in VTA Baron Samedi leads a clan of vampires. This has made my mind spin, any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T07:22:59-08:00","id":1032118,"title":"","content":"The loa Baron Samedi isn't the vampire Baron Samedi.<br /> The Loa are perceived as spirits by the Dreamspeakers. While there could be a relationship between this particular spirit and the vampire, this does not need to be adressed in the game.<br /> <br /> Or the vampire bloodline doesn't exist in your game.<br /> <br /> This is one of the problems with crossover, or at least &quot;canon&quot; crossover. Everyone it's fighting to have all the cool real life icons for their game, so you will necessarily end with &quot;people&quot; that it's claimed by various splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T08:39:15-08:00","id":1032144,"title":"","content":"The <i>Book of Crafts'</i> Bata'a description has no mention of Samedi vampires, as far as I remember. Baron Samedi is mentioned as granting Life, Entropy and divination effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:45:36-08:00","id":1032174,"title":"","content":"There is also a Baron Samedi for Wraith, which is different from the one for Mage and the one for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:51:35-08:00","id":1032179,"title":"","content":"It's actually probably even worse than that. Wraith has Loa too. They are the wraiths of the Caribbean (<i>Les Invisibles</i>) who have made pacts with <i>Les Mysteres</i>, beings of the Tempest who have great power who are otherwise about as vague as vague can be. The Loa aren't Les Mysteres, so they used to be regular folks. So Baron Samedi is also probably a wraith of significant power as well. (Which begs the question of who, exactly, he was before he died.) And it's really hard not to factor this in as the entirety of the Ghede <i>nanchon </i>is about as Shadowlands aspected as any group of supernatural agencies can be. <br /> <br /> So you've got the renegade 4th gen (?) Cappadocian derivative who started his own bloodline walking around Haiti.<br /> <br /> The empowered soul of some dead guy who is ruling over a court of powerful wraiths (the Ghede) in the Mirrorlands.<br /> <br /> And you have a spirit of some variety, probably High Umbra, that is also a Loa, and also Baron Samedi. Or maybe a bunch of different High Umbral spirits that represent different Barons (not out of line with the different Barons or aspects of the Baron or close relatives/co-rulers of the Ghede that are present in Voudoun - Papa Ghede, Baron Cimitiere, Baron La Croix, Baron Kriminel, etc.)<br /> <br /> You're going to have to handle it the way Aleph suggests and pick one, deal with some cognitive dissonace (yup, lots of Barons out there...), or find some ways to reconcile them.... Maybe the vampire is one of the aspects of the Baron that is considered permanently manifested on this side of the Shroud, the Loa of the Mirrorlands is the opposite and the other aspects are the more Umbral sorts... So there might be ocaisional meet and greets between one Baron and another or even small conclaves of some (or all?) of the Barons from time to time to deal with Baron business. (&quot;Let the Baron La Croix call the meeting to order? Shall we forgo with the reading of the minutes of the last meeting? Etc.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:58:26-08:00","id":1032281,"title":"","content":"I think that there are five types of Baron Samedi. There is the 4th generation Kindred associated with the Samedi, there is the God of the High Umbra, there is the Wraith of the Low Umbra, there is probably a Spirit in the Middle Umbra that goes by the name of Baron Samedi, and there is probably an entity of the Dreaming that goes by the name of Baron Samedi. There may be even more types of Baron Samedi out there (Fera, Kindred, Mages, etc), the point though is that there does not have to be just one. Baron Samedi is an archetype, and there are going to always be entities that take the name of archetypes because of the power that it gives them (who was the first Baron Samedi, however, depends on your perspective).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:34:30-08:00","id":1032301,"title":"","content":"Well, as far a the WOD goes... you can make up more if you want but have three - Wraith Loa Baron Samedi, Samedi bloodline vamp Baron Samedi, Ba'ata Loa Baron Samedi (presumably High Umbra... because, &quot;Mage&quot;).<br /> <br /> There are infinite nigh High Umbra and Dreaming Baron Samedi, since that's every different dream people might have of the good Baron and every persistent conceptualization of every version of the Baron from the Touton Macou to James Bond to, probably, some giggling cartoon version bastardized down to a kid's cartoon. <br /> <br /> Middle Umbra? Well... probably some Jaggling and/or Incarnae of relative concepts look, act and maybe even call themselves the Baron....<br /> <br /> So will the real Baron please stand up? <br /> <br /> Good luck with that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:47:10-08:00","id":1032309,"title":"","content":"I can imagine a Marauder going around trying to collect all the various incarnations of Baron Samedi, for a Samedi Party","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:47:00-08:00","id":1032655,"title":"","content":"The Vampire Samedi are explicitly using the preestablished concept of the Baron to cover their concept. The Dreamspeaker might find them to be fellows on the same path or abominations abusing the sacred name of the Baron. depending on the character. Suffice to say he's going to readily see they aren't something he's getting power from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:56:25-08:00","id":1032693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1032655#post1032655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vampire Samedi are explicitly using the preestablished concept of the Baron to cover their concept. The Dreamspeaker might find them to be fellows on the same path or abominations abusing the sacred name of the Baron. depending on the character. Suffice to say he's going to readily see they aren't something he's getting power from.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may say that (in the White Wolf materials), but the (vampire) Baron seems to be rather old, probably one of the very early African slaves brought over to replace the dying/dead indigenous native Caribbeans (particularly when examining the ages of his childer), and the whole Gede <i>nanchon </i>seems to be indigenous to the New World (there isn't really a comparable member of the Orisha unlike the Rada <i>nanchon</i>). meaning there might not have been an &quot;idea&quot; (Upper) or &quot;visceral&quot; (Middle) spiritual version until about the same time as the other two Barons were around. It seems likely that the wraith Baron and the vampire Baron probably have a lot to do with the perception of the WOD Loa Baron. Which is what will shape the/any spiritual version (whether Middle or, especially, Upper Umbral).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:57:35-08:00","id":1032807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires#post1032109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've run into a dilemma.<br /> <br /> My dreamspeaker is a Haitian bokor with a deep affinity for the Loa. Lately, he's been asking them for help and to become his allies and so on. I've been interested in soliciting baron samedi, the Haitian deity of death as one of his allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Problem is, apparently in VTA Baron Samedi leads a clan of vampires. This has made my mind spin, any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this scary vision that many Sorcerers and Mages in the Caribbean let in or trust people who <i>truthfully</i> &quot;serve Baron Samedi&quot; or &quot;have utmost respect for the Baron&quot;...only to get pulled into the webs of Samedi vampires, or killed by them. The Bata'a might even assume that the Loa Baron has some kind of power over the name, and the Samedi will be easily punished for this slight...only to be surprised by the fact that the Cainite Baron Samedi is older than the Loa, and in fact has the upper hand in the metaphysics concerning the name and associated concepts. (Your Dreamspeaker could investigate and try to change this.)<br /> Effects and rotes calling upon the Loa Baron might not work against Samedi vampires and their Ghouls. The Samedi could have an Obfuscate (or Obfuscate+Presence) power that fools any mind reading or divinations so that they show up as faithful servants of the Loa Baron Samedi.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Loa Baron could have existed before, but under a different name and form. Also - the relation between the different Barons doesn't have to be antagonistic. So the Loa Baron might require your Dreamspeaker to become a Ghoul to a Samedi for a period of time (a few months, or a few years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-24-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:52:04-08:00","id":1032853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1032807#post1032807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, the Loa Baron could have existed before, but under a different name and form. Also - the relation between the different Barons doesn't have to be antagonistic. So the Loa Baron might require your Dreamspeaker to become a Ghoul to a Samedi for a period of time (a few months, or a few years).</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea.... I find it interesting. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the Les Invisibles Loa Baron Samedi might demand a period of serving as a cheval for one of his Ghede entourage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:08:18-08:00","id":1032864,"title":"","content":"Perhaps he (my haitian dreamspeaker) could just barter with other Loa, as it seems Baron Samedi may just be tied down with the caanites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:01:48-08:00","id":1033007,"title":"","content":"If it's a Mage game, I'd go with Baron Samedi being a powerful umbral spirit, verging on godhood. Given that he's the loa of resurrection, I think Haitian folklore writes checks a wraith or vampire couldn't cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:22:39-08:00","id":1033023,"title":"","content":"Loa of Resurrection? Do you have a source for that? Everything I've seen is about death and the dead. That's the whole purview of the Ghede <i>nanchon</i>.<br /> <br /> In Mage,for the purposes of Dreamspeakers/Ba'ata/any other interested magely parties, some/most of the Baron could/should be Umbral, perhaps even a Choir of Barons. Which isn't that different from some of the various versions/aspects/truths of the Good Baron as he is/can be perceived... La Croix, Kriminel, Papa Ghede, etc. <br /> <br /> Oh and that can have something to do with some 5th Generation vampire who is absolutely NOT a Cappadocian (please ignore all the rotting and death obsession...) and/or a ghost Or not. <br /> <br /> The Baron your mage meets might be the Baron he expects to meet... That doesn't mean that's the real Baron or that there is such a thing as a real Baron... They're all real. Or not.<br /> <br /> But, I have to admit, there's a lot of appeal to using the Baron. He's iconic and familiar and accessible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:01:51-08:00","id":1033064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1033023#post1033023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loa of Resurrection? Do you have a source for that? Everything I've seen is about death and the dead. That's the whole purview of the Ghede <i>nanchon</i>.<br /> <br /> In Mage,for the purposes of Dreamspeakers/Ba'ata/any other interested magely parties, some/most of the Baron could/should be Umbral, perhaps even a Choir of Barons. Which isn't that different from some of the various versions/aspects/truths of the Good Baron as he is/can be perceived... La Croix, Kriminel, Papa Ghede, etc.<br /> <br /> Oh and that can have something to do with some 5th Generation vampire who is absolutely NOT a Cappadocian (please ignore all the rotting and death obsession...) and/or a ghost Or not.<br /> <br /> The Baron your mage meets might be the Baron he expects to meet... That doesn't mean that's the real Baron or that there is such a thing as a real Baron... They're all real. Or not.<br /> <br /> But, I have to admit, there's a lot of appeal to using the Baron. He's iconic and familiar and accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of things would you foresee a dreamspeaker who got Baron into a fetish or got him as an ally doing with him? Do you think his powers wouldn't work on vamps or anything of the sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:06:13-08:00","id":1033065,"title":"","content":"I think one of the Blood Magic books specifically mentions a Baron Samedi as some kind of god that has a Lasombra worshipper. He can insta grant you some sort of Necromancy Path magic but the Lasombra will tell you to your face it isn't worth the price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T22:02:13-08:00","id":1033150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1032693#post1032693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They may say that (in the White Wolf materials), but the (vampire) Baron seems to be rather old, probably one of the very early African slaves brought over to replace the dying/dead indigenous native Caribbeans (particularly when examining the ages of his childer), and the whole Gede <i>nanchon </i>seems to be indigenous to the New World (there isn't really a comparable member of the Orisha unlike the Rada <i>nanchon</i>). meaning there might not have been an &quot;idea&quot; (Upper) or &quot;visceral&quot; (Middle) spiritual version until about the same time as the other two Barons were around. It seems likely that the wraith Baron and the vampire Baron probably have a lot to do with the perception of the WOD Loa Baron. Which is what will shape the/any spiritual version (whether Middle or, especially, Upper Umbral).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or he may have been a native concept that was incorporated into the faith from interaction with Native Caribbeans. There's also the whole matter of mystery of the Samedi in general in Vampire, but suffice to say the actual Baron(Vampire) doesn't claim to be a Loa so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:09:12-08:00","id":1033631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1033023#post1033023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loa of Resurrection? Do you have a source for that? Everything I've seen is about death and the dead. That's the whole purview of the Ghede <i>nanchon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://Gruesome Critters, and Beasts from the Darkside\" target=\"_blank\">Brad Steiger's <i>Real Monsters, Gruesome Critters, and Beasts from the Darkside</i></a> for one, though I've heard it elsewhere as well. It's not his most iconic sphere of influence, but he is invoked for healing as well as destructive purposes.<br /> <br /> I may crack open my Zora Neale Hurston books later in the week to see if I can track down something from a more closely involved source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 01-17-2017, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:52:32-08:00","id":1033663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1032853#post1032853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the Les Invisibles Loa Baron Samedi might demand a period of serving as a cheval for one of his Ghede entourage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Appropriate, especially considering how a cheval for Baron Samedi-related spirit might be very grimly and/or roughly treated. Tending (or creating) Wraith Fetters or Passions might also be demanded.<br /> The shadows of the Wraith Loas are described as being somehow subdued in their self-destructive impulses, but still being detrimental. Baron Samedi related Les Invisibles could be very dark and spectral while still being Wraiths. Focusing on the Underworld is definitely fitting for a Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1033065#post1033065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the Blood Magic books specifically mentions a Baron Samedi as some kind of god that has a Lasombra worshipper. He can insta grant you some sort of Necromancy Path magic but the Lasombra will tell you to your face it isn't worth the price.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in <i>Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy</i>. He seems to be the Loa Baron Samedi. He is described as feeling contempt and amusement towards vampires. \u201c<i>Still seeking Samedi's approval, she promised to bring a legion of Cainite who would become his houngans. At this news he laughed until acrid tears flowed down his cheeks.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> If you go with multiple Barons, it's possible that it's the Wraith Baron who is tormenting the Lasombra. His appearences are Embody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-24-2018, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:00:43-08:00","id":1033667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1033150#post1033150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or he may have been a native concept that was incorporated into the faith from interaction with Native Caribbeans. There's also the whole matter of mystery of the Samedi in general in Vampire, but suffice to say the actual Baron(Vampire) doesn't claim to be a Loa so...</div> </div> </div> </div>No evidence of anything remotely like Samedi or the Ghede in Taino or Carib mythology or legends insofar as we have them. (Which is more than a little and less than enough...) There's an outlier Orisha (of smallpox) that seems tangentially relevant, but not as a Baron precursor/alternate ID, more as the one lone guy who seems to be anything like any of the Ghede at all.<br /> <br /> If the Samedi Baron Samedi shows up at a ceremony and says &quot;I am the Baron Samedi and you all should do the sorts of things that I as the Baron Samedi am supposed to want to you to do&quot; then he's acting like a Loa. And there's definitely some evidence that he (and other Samedi) do so (and or act as other Ghede Loa, vide Brigitte). Calling himself by the name of the Loa is acting like the Loa. If he had the name first but is still using it as acting out the part as per the Loa, he's acting like he's a Loa. Saying he's not claiming to be a Loa is nitpicking to the level of sophistry. If he didn't want to claim to be the Loa with the exact same name, he'd have everyone calling him &quot;Ted&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:02:52-08:00","id":1033668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1033631#post1033631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://Gruesome Critters, and Beasts from the Darkside\" target=\"_blank\">Brad Steiger's <i>Real Monsters, Gruesome Critters, and Beasts from the Darkside</i></a> for one, though I've heard it elsewhere as well. It's not his most iconic sphere of influence, but he is invoked for healing as well as destructive purposes.<br /> <br /> I may crack open my Zora Neale Hurston books later in the week to see if I can track down something from a more closely involved source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never ever seen this in any of the materials I've got on hand or have read in the scholarly vein. Including some stuff from the '20s that has some really really really creepy pictures...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T11:25:42-07:00","id":1344230,"title":"","content":"Another question:<br /> <br /> Is Vampiric voodun (like Wanga Sorcery) similar/superior to a Mage's baa'ta voodoo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:13:03-07:00","id":1344252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032109-baron-samedi-dreamspeakers-vampires?p=1344230#post1344230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question:<br /> <br /> Is Vampiric voodun (like Wanga Sorcery) similar/superior to a Mage's baa'ta voodoo?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lets assume Magic is a tree. Hedge magic is the base and True Magick are branches with leaves. True Magick builts on hedge magic allowing it to grow and change. Blood magic is.. a parasite that grows from the Tree. its has the same base but doesn't enrich or grow the tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}